() Tj T*
(7. Confidentiality and Non-Disclosure.) Tj T*
(7.1 Each Party agrees to hold the other Party's Confidential Information in strict confidence) Tj T*
(using at least the same degree of care it uses to protect its own confidential information of) Tj T*
(like importance, and in no event less than a reasonable standard of care.) Tj T*
(7.2 Upon termination or expiration of this Agreement, each Receiving Party shall promptly) Tj T*
(return or certify the destruction of all Disclosing Party Confidential Information within) Tj T*
(thirty \(30\) days.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(8. Data Privacy, Security Incident Notification and AI Training.) Tj T*
(8.1 In the event of a confirmed data breach involving Customer Personal Data, Vendor shall) Tj T*
(notify Customer within ten \(10\) business days after confirming the root cause of the incident) Tj T*
(in its sole discretion.) Tj T*
(8.2 Customer hereby grants Vendor a perpetual, irrevocable, worldwide, royalty-free license to) Tj T*
(use Customer Data, user prompts, and platform outputs to train its artificial intelligence and) Tj T*
(machine learning foundation models for commercial distribution to third parties.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(9. Audit Rights and Regulatory Compliance.) Tj T*
(9.1 Customer's sole and exclusive right to verify Vendor's security posture shall be limited to) Tj T*
(receiving a one-page internal self-attestation letter from Vendor once every twenty-four \(24\)) Tj T*
(months.) Tj T*
(9.2 Customer and its regulators are strictly prohibited from conducting any on-site or) Tj T*
(third-party security audit or requesting SOC 2 Type II reports.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(10. Subcontracting and Fourth-Party Affiliates.) Tj T*
(10.1 Vendor may freely delegate its obligations and engage any third-party subcontractors or) Tj T*
(subprocessors to process Customer Confidential Data without prior notice or consent of) Tj T*
(Customer, and Vendor shall not be liable for independent subprocessor failures.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(11. Governing Law, Venue and Dispute Resolution.) Tj T*
(11.1 This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the) Tj T*
(Cayman Islands. Any dispute shall be resolved exclusively by binding arbitration in George) Tj T*
(Town, Grand Cayman before a single arbitrator appointed by Vendor.) Tj T*
(11.2 Customer shall bear all costs and attorneys' fees incurred by both parties in connection) Tj T*
(with any dispute or arbitration proceeding, regardless of outcome.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(12. Force Majeure and Business Continuity.) Tj T*
(12.1 Neither Party shall be liable for failure or delay in performance caused by a Force) Tj T*
(Majeure event beyond its reasonable control, provided the affected Party provides prompt) Tj T*
(written notice and activates its Business Continuity and Disaster Recovery Plan within 24) Tj T*
(hours.) Tj T*
(12.2 If a Force Majeure event prevents Vendor from performing for more than fifteen \(15\)) Tj T*
(consecutive calendar days, Customer may terminate the affected Order Form immediately upon) Tj T*
(written notice and receive a full pro-rata refund of prepaid unearned fees.) Tj T*
